Ticket #4471 combined reports about dates shown on the wrong day. The export has overlapping
rows, so counts below deduplicate by report ID before grouping.

## Problems

The reports split into two causes. The intake tag is only a guess; the tenant locale, booking
form, and channel determine the cause.

### Shared parser reads dates month first

For tenants whose locale writes the day before the month, the shared parser flipped day and month.
This cause appears across app, email, and booking-v2 form reports. The reports in this group
are tracked in [the shared parser ticket](https://github.com/sebadab1/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2).

### booking-v3 hint conflicts with day-first locales

The booking-v3 form told people to enter month first, while its tenant locale reads dates day
first. This separate form-hint problem affects booking-v3 form reports only. The reports are
tracked in [the booking-v3 hint ticket](https://github.com/sebadab1/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1);
do not merge it with the shared parser issue.

## Engineering outcome

The [course desk update](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows), checked on 10 November
2026, marks #4471 closed on 05 October with two different outcomes:

- **Parser — FIXED:** engineering reports `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`.
  The shared parser ticket is closed as completed.
- **Hint — WON'T FIX:** engineering reports `booking-v3 form retired`.
  The booking-v3 hint ticket is closed as not planned, not as a shipped hint fix.

These are the course's reported engineering outcomes, not production changes made in this repo.
The report counts below describe the original export; closing a problem does not remove its
historical reports.

